{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph stored as an incidence list: a row per hyperedge of its members and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row per vertex of its memberships. The undirected counterpart of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":", named as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedAdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":" is. ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", the bit-matrix representation, is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"undirected one of its pair, because “oriented incidence matrix” is the established name of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other.)"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndirectedIncidenceList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices are any "},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" values, kept in an "},{"code":"OrderedSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose element "},{"code":"i","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index "},{"code":"i","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the vertices listed first, then new members by first appearance, as "},{"code":"LabeledGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"assigns them. A hyperedge is a set of vertices of any size, the empty set included; repeated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyperedges are kept, each at its own position "},{"code":"0..<hyperedgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and a member listed twice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is stored once. Members are stored in vertex-index order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage is compressed sparse rows: the members of every hyperedge in one array, and for every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex its incidence numbers and, beside them, its hyperedge positions, in rows of shared"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pools. So "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedges(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are stored "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ArraySlice<Int>"},{"type":"text","text":" rows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read without hashing, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hypergraph makes a constant number of allocations however many vertices it has. Every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex-space read hashes its vertex once; index-space reads and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" algorithms"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hash none."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Hyperedges can be appended but not removed (removal, and with it a decision on positions, is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left for later). Equality ignores the order of the vertices and of the hyperedges.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:11Hypergra